Selecta AdPlug replayer module (plugins/replayers/adplug)
=========================================================

This module statically links AdPlug and libbinio, so the combined module is distributed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version. It is built only with -DSELECTA_GPL_PLUGINS=ON as a
separate loadable module; the Selecta core never links it and stays MIT. The adapter and shim sources in this directory
are MIT like the core and are also usable under the LGPL as part of this module.

Licence count of the vendored code (third_party/adplug, third_party/libbinio), checked file by file:

  - AdPlug player sources (src/*.cpp, *.h): LGPL-2.1-or-later. Count of files with a GPL-only licence: 0.
  - adl.cpp / adl.h (Westwood ADL, derived from ScummVM): dual GPL-2.0-or-later / LGPL; taken under the LGPL.
  - jbm.cpp: LGPL header, but a comment says "Released under the terms of the GNU General Public License". Either
    reading is compatible with this GPL-opt-in module.
  - depack.c / depack.h (aPLib depacker, Joergen Ibsen): the header says only "Copyright (c) 1998-2014 Joergen Ibsen,
    All Rights Reserved" with no licence text; aPLib itself is freeware (free use and redistribution, commercial
    included, per its own licence file which is not vendored). Unresolved: confirm before any non-GPL-opt-in use.
  - Nuked OPL3 (nukedopl.c / nukedopl.h, Nuke.YKT): LGPL-2.1-or-later. This is the only OPL emulator built in.
  - libbinio (src/*.cpp, *.h): LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Full texts: third_party/adplug/COPYING and third_party/libbinio/COPYING. Authors: third_party/adplug/AUTHORS and
third_party/libbinio/AUTHORS. Pinned revisions: third_party/adplug/REVISION and third_party/libbinio/REVISION.
